---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
// About (skeleton v0.3 §3.9), rebuilt from the operator's own first-pass copy
// (A-18) — pricing analogies restored (A-18 amends A-8), the pretentious Doer
// opener removed. Adapted to the full stack: the legacy version was
// marketing-only, so the CRM + dashboard are woven into the "what we do" and
// "heavy lifting" paragraphs ("the other stuff"). A-4: operator's personal
// track record is personal credibility, never an SBP-ownership claim.
// Closing line LOCKED.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The story behind Slow Boil Productions — built by a spirits brand owner who hit the marketing wall and built the marketing and the tools he wished existed.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap a-top">
      <span class="eyebrow">// Built by a spirits brand owner</span>
      <h1>I’ve been on both sides of the wall.</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap a-body prose">
      <p class="lead">Nobody builds a brand because they want to become a marketer.</p>

      <p>You built something real — a product you believe in, a vision you’ve been carrying for years. And then you hit the wall every developing brand hits: the marketing wall. The place where passion meets budget, and budget usually wins.</p>

      <p>The agencies want $20,000 a month. The freelancers disappear after two invoices. The DIY tools look simple until you’re three hours deep into a Canva template at midnight, wondering why nothing looks the way it did in your head.</p>

      <p><strong>I know that wall. I’ve been on both sides of it.</strong></p>

      <hr />

      <p>Slow Boil Productions was built on one belief: <em>the brands that deserve to win are losing because of money, not merit.</em></p>

      <p>We use AI the way a master chef uses a sharp knife — not to replace the cook, but to make every cut cleaner and faster. The strategy is still human. The instincts are still earned. But the execution? That’s where we close the gap.</p>

      <p>We work with spirits brands, beverage-alcohol brands, and the developing consumer brands coming up behind them — anyone tired of being told they have to spend a fortune to look like they belong.</p>

      <p>We do product photography that looks like it came from a $50,000 studio shoot. We build websites that convert. We run digital marketing that actually moves product. We train AI on your brand so every asset feels like <em>you</em> — not a stock photo with your logo slapped on it. And underneath the marketing run the same tools I use on my own brands: a CRM that knows what a depletion is, and a dashboard that tells you what actually moved.</p>

      <p>And we charge what’s fair. Not what the market will bear. What’s actually fair.</p>

      <hr />

      <p>I built this for you. Because nobody should have to pay $500,000 to learn what I already know.</p>

      <p>We use AI to do the heavy lifting so we can offer you real, professional marketing — and the real, professional tools to run on — at a price point that won’t drain your tank before you ever get to market.</p>

      <p>We don’t want you as a client forever. <strong>We want to grow you to the point where you’re too big for us — and when that day comes, we’re going to celebrate it.</strong></p>

      <p>That’s the slow boil. The moment right before everything changes.</p>

      <p class="a-close">You didn’t come this far to fold. Let’s get to work.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Built for our world. By someone in it.</h2>

      <p>Most AI marketing tools are built by tech people who saw AI and decided to make a product. They don’t know that you can’t run alcohol ads in dry counties. They don’t know that distributor relationships are the actual lifeblood. They don’t know what depletion means.</p>

      <p><strong>I do. Because I’m running spirits brands every day.</strong></p>

      <p>Every win, every failure, every weird thing I learn about a distributor or a state regulation or a content format that’s working — it all feeds back into Slow Boil overnight. The system you hire today is smarter tomorrow.</p>

      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary a-cta">Get in touch →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .a-top { max-width: 46rem; }
    .a-top h1 { margin-top: var(--s2); max-width: 15ch; }
    .a-body { margin-top: var(--s7); max-width: 720px; }
    .a-body .lead { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-lg); color: var(--text); margin-bottom: var(--s5); max-width: none; }
    .a-body hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: var(--s6) 0; }
    .a-body h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-h3); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: var(--s4); }
    .a-close { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-lg); font-style: italic; color: var(--text); margin-top: var(--s5); }
    .a-cta { margin-top: var(--s6); width: fit-content; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
